+/* I51_INS (NAME, ARGS, SIZE, BIN, MASK): the instruction NAME with the
+   three operands ARGS, SIZE bytes long, whose first byte B has
+   (B & MASK) == BIN.  The rows of one mnemonic are adjacent, and no two
+   rows match the same first byte.
+
+   The operand letters:
+     N	none
+     A	A
+     C	AB
+     r	C
+     P	DPTR
+     T	@DPTR
+     @	@A+DPTR
+     X	@A+PC
+     R	R0..R7, in the opcode byte
+     I	@R0 or @R1, in the opcode byte
+     D	a direct address
+     B	a bit address
+     /	a complemented bit address
+     #	an immediate, two bytes after DPTR and one elsewhere
+     J	a relative branch target
+     1	an 11-bit code address, three bits of it in the opcode byte
+     6	a 16-bit code address
+
+   The fields follow the opcode byte in operand order, except that
+   MOV direct,direct stores its source first.  */
